# Citation

If you use youtube-live-ultra in academic research, please cite:

```bibtex
@software{youtube_live_ultra,
  author = {Aymeric, hexapost-studio},
  title = {YouTube Live Ultra — Low-latency YouTube live streaming tool},
  year = {2026},
  version = {1.0.0},
  url = {https://github.com/hexapost-studio/youtube-live-ultra},
  note = {Uses HLS edge=1 with mpv hardware decode for 2-5x lower latency
          than the YouTube web player. Triple fallback architecture
          (streamlink → yt-dlp → mpv --ytdl).}
}
```

## Related academic references

The project builds on:

- Bentaleb, Begen, Zimmermann et al. "Toward One-Second Latency: Evolution of Live Media Streaming." IEEE COMST 2025. [arXiv:2310.03256](https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.03256)
- Liu, Jia, Jiang, Zhang et al. "Camel: Frame-Level Bandwidth Estimation for Low-Latency Live Streaming." WWW 2026. [arXiv:2602.09500](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.09500)
- Menon, Zhu, Rajendran et al. "Optimal Quality and Efficiency in Adaptive Live Streaming with JND-Aware Low Latency Encoding." MHV 2024. [arXiv:2401.15343](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.15343)
